-
-    TASK:
-    Score all frozen candidate pairs with each MODEL_SPEC through local llama.cpp CUDA inference.
-    Measure the conditional log-likelihood margin between the exact compatible sequence and its
-    matched violation. Emit atom and joint margins. Fit no probe. Use no LLM judge.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: call cached_sota_pair(); require all three exact GGUF files and hashes, native
-       tokenizer metadata, token log-probability support, CUDA, task-owned exclusive GPU leases, free
-       ports, sufficient disk, both Exp6836 readiness fields equal to 1, and a one-pair live canary
-       per model. Observe but never interrupt unrelated processes. Write
-       complete_blocked_output_free_compatibility with gate_check_summary and exact values on failure.
-    1. Add REQ-CONSTRAINT-6837 and tests before implementation. Test forced-sequence scoring, token
-       alignment, prompt masking, equal-token pairing, raw receipts, checkpoint restart, model
-       isolation, process ownership, and clean teardown.
-    2. Run one task-owned model process at a time. Record command, PID, process start, port, GPU UUID,
-       visible devices, model hash, tokenizer hash, first score, final score, and teardown.
-    3. Score each fixed sequence without sampling, repair, generation, grammar, or answer feedback.
-       Store every token id and token log-probability used in each margin.
-    4. Checkpoint bounded batches. On restart, verify row hashes and run only missing row identities.
-       Never regenerate complete rows.
-    5. Report margins by model, atom family, obligation count, compatible label position, prompt
-       length, candidate length, and permutation. Do not pool models as exchangeable samples.
-    6. Set obligation_compatibility_stream_ready_score from receipt and row completeness only. Keep
-       any effect estimate separate. A lower compatible-sequence energy is not proof of truth.
-    7. Run focused tests, ruff, OpenSpec coverage, adversarial verification, artifact convention
-       audit, verdict-row consistency lint, CUDA authenticity checks, and root-clutter checks.
-    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles; preconditions_checked;
-       inference_substrate (live_local_llama_cpp_cuda_forced_sequence_scoring); duration_s;
-       model_specs (all three exact MODEL_SPECS); models_used; model_artifact_hashes;
-       tokenizer_receipts; process_receipts; accelerator_samples; random_seed;
-       source_artifact_hashes; reproducibility_checksum; rows (one model and candidate pair with raw
-       token ids, token log-probabilities, scores, labels, lengths, and margin); per_model_results;
-       per_atom_results; joint_results; shortcut_control_cells; checkpoint_manifest;
-       method_parity_limits; obligation_compatibility_stream_ready_score (exact field consumed by
-       Exp6838); gate_check_summary (failed check and observed value for any blocked verdict);
-       verifier_is_oracle (false, Exp6836 exact labels are external); verdict_class (positive |
-       circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal,
-       row-supported, and prefixed complete_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6837_three_family_output_free_compatibility.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
